module

public import Sheaf.Paper.IntegralConstructibleLinear
public import Sheaf.Paper.SfIntegralConstructibleTriangulated
public import Sheaf.Paper.CompletedIntegralCoefficientGerm
public import Sheaf.NumberTheory.Padics.CoefficientExtensionFinite
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic

/-!
# Constant-section linearity of the intrinsic integral constructible category

Source: Weil blueprint, `def-weil-rationalization-karoubi`, order 1460, the integral
linearity prerequisite (blueprint: lem-weil-integral-constructible-linear).

The ambient constant-section action is the published `integralCoefficientLinear`.
The full subcategory here is the currently recorded `sfIntegralConstructibleCategory`,
with the triangulation of `SfIntegralConstructibleTriangulated`. Legacy declarations
remain available through the public import.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace WeilConjectures

variable (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime] (E : Type u) [Field E]
  [Algebra ℚ_[l] E] [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[l] E]
  (Y : AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.{u})

/-- The published ambient constant-section action, exposed at the source-category
abbreviation used by the intrinsic constructible predicate. The two module categories
and their standard derived localizations are definitionally identical.
Source: Weil blueprint, order 1460, the integral-linearity prerequisite
(blueprint: lem-weil-integral-constructible-linear). -/
noncomputable instance sfIntegralCoefficientLinear :
    Linear (Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E)
      (DerivedCategory (scalarReductionSource l E Y)) :=
  integralCoefficientLinear l E Y

/-- The intrinsic full subcategory inherits precisely the ambient constant-section
module structure on Hom groups, including its bilinear composition.
Source: Weil blueprint, order 1460, the integral-linearity prerequisite
(blueprint: lem-weil-integral-constructible-linear). -/
noncomputable instance sfIntegralConstructibleLinear :
    Linear (Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E) (sfIntegralConstructibleCategory l E Y) :=
  Linear.fullSubcategory (sfIntegralConstructible l E Y)

/-- The ambient and intrinsic integral constructible categories are linear for the
canonical constant-section action, and all their integer shifts are linear. The
subcategory has the inherited triangulation and its inclusion preserves scalars.
Source: Weil blueprint, `def-weil-rationalization-karoubi`, order 1460; Stacks
Tags 09MJ, 03CW, 03DA and 05RU
(blueprint: lem-weil-integral-constructible-linear).

Proof (the five steps of the DAG):
1. Apply clause (2) of `lem-pod-adic-limit-finite-modules` to the rank-one module
O_E. It is generated by 1, so the canonical map O_E to the inverse limit of its
finite quotient rings is bijective. It is a ring isomorphism since the quotient
maps preserve addition and multiplication, and limit operations are coordinatewise.
2. For each site object U, the classes of a in the positive finite quotients give
compatible constant sections. The sectionwise inverse limit gives c_U(a), uniquely
specified by these residues (`integralScalarConstant`). These are unital ring maps,
natural under restriction; at the terminal object they give the asserted map to
global sections. Equivalently use the cone defining `integralConstantToCompletion`.
No identification with the discrete constant integral sheaf is required.
3. On module-sheaf morphisms put (a f)_U(x) = c_U(a) f_U(x). The completed ring is
commutative, since every finite quotient is commutative. Thus these maps are module
maps. The compatibility of c with restriction gives naturality. Module identities
hold sectionwise. Module-linearity of g gives g (a f) = a (g f) = (a g) f, proving
bilinearity. The module-sheaf category is abelian in the recorded site universe.
4. Apply `lem-weil-linear-abelian-derived-category`: localization and integer shifts
are linear for this action. On a complex K, multiplication by c_U(a) is the chain
map a id_K. Localization carries it to a id_QK. Bilinearity then gives the displayed
formula for every derived morphism, including those introduced by localization.
This is the published, uniquely characterized `integralCoefficientLinear` action.
5. `sfIntegralConstructibleCategory` is the full subcategory specified by
`def-weil-derived-complete-integral-detailed`. Restrict the ambient Hom module
structures, as in `sfIntegralConstructibleLinear`. The currently recorded
`lem-weil-integral-constructible-triangulated` supplies its inherited shifts and
triangulation. The shift maps are the ambient shift maps on underlying morphisms,
so their scalar identities restrict to the subcategory, as does the inclusion's
linearity. No new boundedness, Tor-dimension or coefficient hypothesis is imposed. -/
theorem sfIntegralConstructible_linear :
    (∀ (a : Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E)
      (K L : DerivedCategory (scalarReductionSource l E Y)) (f : K ⟶ L),
      a • f = (integralScalarDerivedAction l E Y a).app K ≫ f) ∧
    (∀ n : ℤ, Functor.Linear (Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E)
      (shiftFunctor (DerivedCategory (scalarReductionSource l E Y)) n)) ∧
    Functor.Linear (Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E) (sfIntegralConstructible l E Y).ι ∧
    (∀ n : ℤ, Functor.Linear (Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E)
      (shiftFunctor (sfIntegralConstructibleCategory l E Y) n)) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, inferInstance, ?_⟩
  · exact (integralCoefficientLinear_existsUnique l E Y).exists.choose_spec
  · intro n
    exact integralCoefficientShift_linear l E Y n
  · intro n
    let P := sfIntegralConstructible l E Y
    let R := Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E
    let : (shiftFunctor (DerivedCategory (scalarReductionSource l E Y)) n).Linear R :=
      integralCoefficientShift_linear l E Y n
    let : (shiftFunctor P.FullSubcategory n ⋙ P.ι).Linear R :=
      Functor.linear_of_iso R (P.ι.commShiftIso n).symm
    constructor
    intro X Z f a
    apply P.ι.map_injective
    rw [P.ι.map_smul]
    exact (shiftFunctor P.FullSubcategory n ⋙ P.ι).map_smul a f

/-- Every inherited integer shift is linear for the canonical constant-section action.
This is the final clause of `sfIntegralConstructible_linear`.
Source: Weil blueprint, order 1460, the integral-linearity prerequisite
(blueprint: lem-weil-integral-constructible-linear). -/
noncomputable instance sfIntegralConstructibleShift_linear (n : ℤ) :
    (shiftFunctor (sfIntegralConstructibleCategory l E Y) n).Linear
      (Padic.coefficientExtensionIntegers l E) :=
  (sfIntegralConstructible_linear l E Y).2.2.2 n

end WeilConjectures
